; Breakage 01: Prose sentence uses an undefined Ubiquitous Language term @{block}
; (Direct echo of Verisectorium Note 30 §3: "rule 14 uses «block» in a sense its definition does not give")
; Expected: `ocamlc` compile error pointing to line 13 of THIS .ud file!

|document[broken-01]
  :context udon-spec

  |term[element].draft.foundation A node with name?, unordered attrs, and ordered children.
    :kind    full-term
    :pos     noun
    |invariant Children are strictly ordered.
    |example An element with one text child.
    Inside a @{block}, every @{element} preserves child order.
